{"id":"telecom~stt_telecom_bn_014","trace":{"trace_id":"stt_telecom_bn_014","synthesis_mode":"combined","asset_reference":{"domain_id":"telecom","domain_version":"v1","workflow_id":"recharge_and_plan","workflow_version":"v1","tool_schema_version":"v1","domain_fingerprint":"9fa1ab9d2849cca3"},"capability_labels":{"AX003-SA006-V004":"Task Following > Goal Completion & Task Recovery > Incomplete Information Recovery","AX005-SA004-V001":"Tool Use > Tool Response Construction > Tool Output Grounding"},"zen_prompt":"You are the customer service representative for TELECOM.\n\nYou handle these workflows. Which one a call turns out to be is something you work out from what the customer says:\n- network_complaint: Diagnose coverage and speed complaints against live network status and raise a field ticket where warranted.\n- recharge_and_plan: Recharge a prepaid number, migrate a plan and explain validity and benefits from the live catalogue.\n\nBusiness context:\n- network_complaint: Indian telecom contact centre. Prepaid recharges, plan migrations, data exhaustion and coverage complaints. Plan changes have cycle rules and network faults have defined resolution windows.\n- recharge_and_plan: Indian telecom contact centre. Prepaid recharges, plan migrations, data exhaustion and coverage complaints. Plan changes have cycle rules and network faults have defined resolution windows.\n\nAuthoritative business rules, by the workflow they bind:\n  [network_complaint]\n  - Known outage first: Where a known outage covers the area, the tool's ETA is quoted and no duplicate ticket is raised.\n  - Diagnose before ticket: A line diagnostic must run before a ticket is raised, so the category is evidenced.\n  - No coverage promises: The agent must not promise coverage improvement beyond the ticket's stated window.\n  - Handset limits: Where the diagnostic reports the handset unsupported, that is stated rather than blamed on the network.\n  [recharge_and_plan]\n  - Catalogue truth: Only plans returned by list_plans may be offered, with the price and validity the tool returns.\n  - Postpaid cycle: A postpaid plan change takes effect from the next billing cycle, never immediately.\n  - No benefit invention: Bundled benefits may only be described where the plan record carries them.\n  - Balance before recharge: Existing balance and validity must be read before a recharge is recommended.\n\nTools available to you (7): apply_recharge, check_network_status, list_plans, lookup_subscriber, raise_network_ticket, run_line_diagnostic, verify_customer_identity\nNot every tool applies to every call. Choosing the wrong one is an error even when the call succeeds.\n\nConversation language: bn-IN. Script policy: NATIVE_WITH_ROMAN_ENGLISH.","model_visible_tools":[{"name":"apply_recharge","description":"Apply a recharge or plan migration to the subscriber.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"msisdn":{"type":"string","pattern":"^MSN-[0-9]{4}$"},"plan_id":{"type":"string"}},"required":["msisdn","plan_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"txn_id":{"type":"string"},"plan_id":{"type":"string"},"amount":{"type":"integer"},"effective":{"type":"string","enum":["immediate","next_cycle"]},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["applied","failed"]}},"required":["txn_id","plan_id","amount","effective","status"]},"consequential":true},{"name":"check_network_status","description":"Retrieve tower status, known outages and congestion for a location.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"msisdn":{"type":"string","pattern":"^MSN-[0-9]{4}$"},"pincode":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{6}$"}},"required":["msisdn","pincode"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pincode":{"type":"string"},"outage":{"type":"string","enum":["none","planned_maintenance","fault","congestion"]},"eta_hours":{"type":"integer"},"towers_affected":{"type":"integer"},"known_issue":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["pinc